{
  "format": 1,
  "name": "protection_slot_abi",
  "spec": ["protection 1", "protection 6.6", "protection 9.5", "protection 15", "protection 16", "protection 18.22"],
  "description": "Test 22: the compiled slot tables of 15: fire slot 10 GetStationEfficiency pops 8 (hidden pointer + occupant) and returns the pointer; police slot 37 GetJailCurrentUpkeepCost pops 4 and returns EDX:EAX (trunc(float(cost 1000) x 0.75) = 750 as int64; 0 without an item); police slot 41 EndJailbreak returns AL = 0 even after ending a jailbreak (the jail leaves the list). The crime simulator's slots: police 5 (+0x14) the uint8 grid, 27 (+0x6C) ResetUnjailedCriminals in EAX, 30 (+0x78) GetJailPopulation, 38 (+0x98) ProcessMonthlyCrimeStats (nothing meaningful); 28/29 are the two GetJailCapacity overloads in reverse order; 26 and 45 slots. QueryInterface answers 1, the class IID, 0x452294AA, 0xC9C00435, 0xE4FDA3D4 and nothing else; class IDs 0x2990C05A / 0x6990C04F. GetStrikingStations appends (fire) and returns 0 without the city flag (police); GetStrikeLength -1 without a date. Values from the 15 tables by hand. SetStationFunding (6.6) uses the item's department, GetDepartmentBudget(item.departmentID), not the simulator's own: an item naming department 0x12345678 sets the funding there; an item whose department lookup fails returns false with no call; no item returns false.",
  "steps": [
    {"op": "protection_create", "kind": "fire"},
    {"op": "protection_env", "tuning": "shipped"},
    {"op": "protection_init"},
    {"op": "protection_call", "method": "slot_count", "expect": 26},
    {"op": "protection_call", "method": "slot", "args": [10], "expect": {"name": "GetStationEfficiency", "pops": 8, "ret": "hidden_ptr"}},
